#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18263
msgid ""
"Quotation mark @@-commands (@code{@@quotedblright@{@}} and the like), are "
"likewise replaced by their Unicode values.  Normal quotation "
"@emph{characters} (e.g., ASCII ` and ') are not altered.  @xref{Inserting "
"Quotation Marks}."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18268
msgid ""
"Any @code{@@acronym}, @code{@@abbr}, @code{@@email}, and @code{@@image} "
"commands are replaced by their first argument.  (For these commands, all "
"subsequent arguments are optional, and ignored here.)  "
"@xref{@code{@@acronym}}, and @ref{@code{@@email}}, and @ref{Images}."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18270
msgid "Accents are handled according to the next section."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18272
msgid "Any other command is an error, and the result is unspecified."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18274
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Xref 8-bit Character Expansion"
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18275
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Cross-reference 8-bit Character Expansion"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18276
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML cross-references @subentry 8-bit character expansion"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18277
#, no-wrap
msgid "8-bit characters, in HTML cross-references"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18278
#, no-wrap
msgid "Expansion of 8-bit characters in HTML cross-references"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18279
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transliteration of 8-bit characters in HTML cross-references"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18287
msgid ""
"Usually, characters other than plain 7-bit ASCII are transformed into the "
"corresponding Unicode code point(s) in Normalization Form@tie{}C, which uses "
"precomposed characters where available.  (This is the normalization form "
"recommended by the W3C and other bodies.)  This holds when that code point "
"is @code{0xffff} or less, as it almost always is."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18290
msgid ""
"These will then be further transformed by the rules above into the string "
"@samp{_@var{hhhh}}, where @var{hhhh} is the code point in hex."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18292
msgid "For example, combining this rule and the previous section:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18296
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@node @@b@{A@} @@TeX@{@} @@u@{B@} @@point@{@}@@enddots@{@}\n"
"@result{} A-TeX-B_0306-_22C6_002e_002e_002e\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18303
msgid ""
"Notice: 1)@tie{}@code{@@enddots} expands to three periods which in turn "
"expands to three @samp{_002e}'s; 2)@tie{}@code{@@u@{B@}} is a `B' with a "
"breve accent, which does not exist as a pre-accented Unicode character, "
"therefore expands to @samp{B_0306} (B with combining breve)."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18310
msgid ""
"When the Unicode code point is above @code{0xffff}, the transformation is "
"@samp{__@var{xxxxxx}}, that is, two leading underscores followed by six hex "
"digits.  Since Unicode has declared that their highest code point is "
"@code{0x10ffff}, this is sufficient.  (We felt it was better to define this "
"extra escape than to always use six hex digits, since the first two would "
"nearly always be zeros.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18322
msgid ""
"This method works fine if the node name consists mostly of ASCII characters "
"and contains only few 8-bit ones.  But if the document is written in a "
"language whose script is not based on the Latin alphabet (for example, "
"Ukrainian), it will create file names consisting almost entirely of "
"@samp{_@var{xxxx}} notations, which is inconvenient and all but unreadable.  "
"To handle such cases, @command{texi2any} offers the "
"@option{--transliterate-file-names} command line option.  This option "
"enables @dfn{transliteration} of node names into ASCII characters for the "
"purposes of file name creation and referencing.  The transliteration is "
"based on phonetic principles, which makes the generated file names more "
"easily understandable."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18323
#, no-wrap
msgid "Normalization Form C, Unicode"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18328
msgid ""
"For the definition of Unicode Normalization Form@tie{}C, see Unicode report "
"UAX#15, @uref{http://www.unicode.org/reports/tr15/}.  Many related documents "
"and implementations are available elsewhere on the web."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18330
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Xref Mismatch"
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18331
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Cross-reference Mismatch"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18332
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML cross-references @subentry mismatch"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18333
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mismatched HTML cross-reference source and target"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18339
msgid ""
"As mentioned earlier (@pxref{HTML Xref Link Basics}), the generating "
"software may need to guess whether a given manual being cross-referenced is "
"available in split or monolithic form---and, inevitably, it might guess "
"wrong.  However, when the @emph{referent} manual is generated, it is "
"possible to handle at least some mismatches."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18345
msgid ""
"In the case where we assume the referent is split, but it is actually "
"available in mono, the only recourse would be to generate a "
"@file{manual_html/} subdirectory full of HTML files which redirect back to "
"the monolithic @file{manual.html}.  Since this is essentially the same as a "
"split manual in the first place, it's not very appealing."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18351
msgid ""
"On the other hand, in the case where we assume the referent is mono, but it "
"is actually available in split, it is possible to use JavaScript to redirect "
"from the putatively monolithic @file{manual.html} to the different "
"@file{manual_html/node.html} files.  Here's an example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18363
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"function redirect() @{\n"
"  switch (location.hash) @{\n"
"    case \"#Node1\":\n"
"      location.replace(\"manual_html/Node1.html#Node1\"); break;\n"
"    case \"#Node2\" :\n"
"      location.replace(\"manual_html/Node2.html#Node2\"); break;\n"
"    @dots{}\n"
"    default:;\n"
"  @}\n"
"@}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18366
msgid "Then, in the @code{<body>} tag of @file{manual.html}:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18369
#, no-wrap
msgid "<body onLoad=\"redirect();\">\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18375
msgid ""
"Once again, this is something the software which generated the "
"@emph{referent} manual has to do in advance, it's not something the software "
"generating the cross-reference in the present manual can control."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18377
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Xref Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18379
msgid "@nodedescription @file{htmlxref.cnf}."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18379
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Cross-reference Configuration: @file{htmlxref.cnf}"
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18381
#, no-wrap
msgid "htmlxref.cnf"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18382
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML cross-references @subentry configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18383
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cross-reference configuration, for HTML"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18384
#, no-wrap
msgid "Configuration, for HTML cross-manual references"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18389
msgid ""
"@command{texi2any} reads a file named @file{htmlxref.cnf} to gather "
"information for cross-references to other manuals in HTML output.  It is "
"looked for in the following directories:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18391
#, no-wrap
msgid "./"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18393
msgid "(the current directory)"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18394
#, no-wrap
msgid "./.texinfo/"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18396
msgid "(under the current directory)"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18397
#, no-wrap
msgid "~/.texinfo/"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18399
msgid "(where @code{~} is the current user's home directory)"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18400
#, no-wrap
msgid "@var{sysconfdir}/texinfo/"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18403
msgid ""
"(where @var{sysconfdir} is the system configuration directory specified at "
"compile-time, e.g., @file{/usr/local/etc})"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18404
#, no-wrap
msgid "@var{datadir}/texinfo/"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18406
msgid "(likewise specified at compile time, e.g., @file{/usr/local/share})"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18412
msgid ""
"All files found are used, with earlier entries overriding later ones.  The "
"Texinfo distribution includes a default file which handles many GNU manuals; "
"it is installed in the last of the above directories, i.e., "
"@file{@var{datadir}/texinfo/htmlxref.cnf}."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18417
msgid ""
"The @code{HTMLXREF_MODE} customization variable can be set to modify how the "
"files are found.  For instance, if set to @samp{none}, no external "
"information is used.  @code{HTMLXREF_FILE} sets the file name to something "
"else than @file{htmlxref.cnf}.  @pxref{HTML Customization Variables}."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18423
msgid ""
"The file is line-oriented.  Lines consisting only of whitespace are "
"ignored.  Comments are indicated with a @samp{#} at the beginning of a line, "
"optionally preceded by whitespace.  Since @samp{#} can occur in URLs (like "
"almost any character), it does not otherwise start a comment."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18426
msgid ""
"Each non-blank non-comment line must be either a @dfn{variable assignment} "
"or @dfn{manual information}."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18428
msgid "A variable assignment line looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18431
#, no-wrap
msgid "@var{varname} = @var{varvalue}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18438
msgid ""
"Whitespace around the @samp{=} is optional and ignored.  The @var{varname} "
"should consist of letters; case is significant.  The @var{varvalue} is an "
"arbitrary string, continuing to the end of the line.  Variables are then "
"referenced with @samp{$@{@var{varname}@}}; variable references can occur in "
"the @var{varvalue}."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18440
msgid "A manual information line looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18443
#, no-wrap
msgid "@var{manual} @var{keyword} @var{urlprefix}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18451
msgid ""
"with @var{manual} the short identifier for a manual, @var{keyword} being one "
"of: @code{mono}, @code{node}, @code{section}, @code{chapter}, and "
"@var{urlprefix} described below.  Variable references can occur only in the "
"@var{urlprefix}.  For example (used in the canonical @file{htmlxref.cnf}):"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18459
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"G = http://www.gnu.org\n"
"GS = $@{G@}/software\n"
"hello mono    $@{GS@}/hello/manual/hello.html\n"
"hello chapter $@{GS@}/hello/manual/html_chapter/\n"
"hello section $@{GS@}/hello/manual/html_section/\n"
"hello node    $@{GS@}/hello/manual/html_node/\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18461
#, no-wrap
msgid "monolithic manuals, for HTML cross-references"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18464
msgid ""
"If the keyword is @code{mono}, @var{urlprefix} gives the host, directory, "
"and file name for @var{manual} as one monolithic file."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18465
#, no-wrap
msgid "split manuals, for HTML cross-references"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18469
msgid ""
"If the keyword is @code{node}, @code{section}, or @code{chapter}, "
"@var{urlprefix} gives the host and directory for @var{manual} split into "
"nodes, sections, or chapters, respectively."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18477
msgid ""
"When available, @command{texi2any} will use the ``corresponding'' value for "
"cross-references between manuals.  That is, when generating monolithic "
"output (@option{--no-split}), the @code{mono} URL will be used, when "
"generating output that is split by node, the @code{node} URL will be used, "
"etc.  However, if a manual is not available in that form, anything that is "
"available can be used.  Here is the search order for each style:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18483
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"node    @result{} node,    section, chapter, mono\n"
"section @result{} section, chapter, node,    mono\n"
"chapter @result{} chapter, section, node,    mono\n"
"mono    @result{} mono,    chapter, section, node\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18485
#, no-wrap
msgid "--node-files@r{, and HTML cross-references}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18489
msgid ""
"These section- and chapter-level cross-manual references can succeed only "
"when the target manual was created using @option{--node-files}; this is the "
"default for split output."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18494
msgid ""
"If you have additions or corrections to the @file{htmlxref.cnf} distributed "
"with Texinfo, please email @email{bug-texinfo@@gnu.org} as usual.  You can "
"get the latest version from "
"@url{http://ftpmirror.gnu.org/@/texinfo/@/htmlxref.cnf}."
msgstr ""

#. type: appendix
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18496 texinfo/texinfo.texi:18498
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@-Command Details"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18498
msgid "@nodedescription Details of the Texinfo @@-commands."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18502
msgid ""
"Here are the details of @@-commands: information about their syntax, a list "
"of commands, and information about where commands can appear."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18504
#, no-wrap
msgid "Command Syntax"
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18505
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@-Command Syntax"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18506
#, no-wrap
msgid "@sortas{at} @@-commands @subentry syntax"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18507
#, no-wrap
msgid "Syntax, of @@-commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18508
#, no-wrap
msgid "Command syntax"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18511
msgid "Texinfo has the following types of @@-command:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18513
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Brace commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18518
msgid ""
"These commands start with @@ followed by a letter or a word, followed by an "
"argument within braces.  For example, the command @code{@@dfn} indicates the "
"introductory or defining use of a term; it is used as follows: @samp{In "
"Texinfo, @@@@-commands are @@dfn@{mark-up@} commands.}"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18519
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Line commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18525
msgid ""
"These commands occupy an entire line.  The line starts with @@, followed by "
"the name of the command (a word); for example, @code{@@center} or "
"@code{@@cindex}.  If no argument is needed, the word is followed by the end "
"of the line.  If there is an argument, it is separated from the command name "
"by a space.  Braces are not used."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18527
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Block commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18535
msgid ""
"These commands are written at the start of a line, with general text on "
"following lines, terminated by a matching @code{@@end} command on a line of "
"its own.  For example, @code{@@example}, then the lines of a coding example, "
"then @code{@@end example}.  Some of these block commands take arguments as "
"line commands do; for example, @code{@@enumerate A} opening an environment "
"terminated by @code{@@end enumerate}.  Here @samp{A} is the argument."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18536
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Symbol insertion commands with no arguments"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18543
msgid ""
"These commands start with @@ followed by a word followed by a left and "
"right- brace.  These commands insert special symbols in the document; they "
"do not take arguments.  Some examples: @code{@@dots@{@}} @result{} "
"@samp{@dots{}}, @code{@@equiv@{@}} @result{} @samp{@equiv{}}, "
"@code{@@TeX@{@}} @result{} `@TeX{}', and @code{@@bullet@{@}} @result{} "
"@samp{@bullet{}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18544
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. Non-alphabetic commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18553
msgid ""
"The names of commands in all of the above categories consist of alphabetic "
"characters, almost entirely in lower-case.  Unlike those, the non-alphabetic "
"commands consist of an @@ followed by a punctuation mark or other character "
"that is not part of the Latin alphabet.  Non-alphabetic commands are almost "
"always part of text within a paragraph.  The non-alphabetic commands include "
"@code{@@@@}, @code{@@@{}, @code{@@@}}, @code{@@.}, @code{@@@kbd{SPACE}}, and "
"most of the accent commands."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18554
#, no-wrap
msgid "6. Miscellaneous commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18562
msgid ""
"There are a handful of commands that don't fit into any of the above "
"categories; for example, the obsolete command @code{@@refill}, which is "
"always used at the end of a paragraph immediately following the final period "
"or other punctuation character.  @code{@@refill} takes no argument and does "
"not require braces.  Likewise, @code{@@tab} used in a @code{@@multitable} "
"block does not take arguments, and is not followed by braces."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18564
#, no-wrap
msgid "Braces and argument syntax"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18574
msgid ""
"Thus, the alphabetic commands fall into classes that have different argument "
"syntaxes.  You cannot tell to which class a command belongs by the "
"appearance of its name, but you can tell by the command's meaning: if the "
"command stands for a glyph, it is in class 4 and does not require an "
"argument; if it makes sense to use the command among other text as part of a "
"paragraph, the command is in class 1 and must be followed by an argument in "
"braces.  The non-alphabetic commands, such as @code{@@:}, are exceptions to "
"the rule; they do not need braces."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18578
msgid ""
"The purpose of having different syntax for commands is to make Texinfo files "
"easier to read, and also to help the GNU Emacs paragraph and filling "
"commands work properly."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18580
#, no-wrap
msgid "Command List"
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18581
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@-Command List"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18582
#, no-wrap
msgid "Alphabetical @@-command list"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18583
#, no-wrap
msgid "List of @@-commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18584
#, no-wrap
msgid "@sortas{at} @@-commands @subentry list of"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18585
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reference to @@-commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18590
msgid ""
"Here is an alphabetical list of the @@-commands in Texinfo.  Square "
"brackets, @t{[}@w{ }@t{]}, indicate optional arguments; an ellipsis, "
"@samp{@dots{}}, indicates repeated text."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18592
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@@var{whitespace}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18595
msgid ""
"An @code{@@} followed by a space, tab, or newline produces a normal, "
"stretchable, interword space.  @xref{Multiple Spaces}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18596
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@!"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18599
msgid ""
"Produce an exclamation point that ends a sentence (usually after an "
"end-of-sentence capital letter).  @xref{Ending a Sentence}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18600
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@\""
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18601
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@'"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18604
msgid ""
"Generate an umlaut or acute accent, respectively, over the next character, "
"as in @\"o and @'o.  @xref{Inserting Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18605
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@&"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18606
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@ampchar@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18608
msgid "Generate an ampersand.  @xref{Inserting an Ampersand}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18611
msgid "Force a line break.  @xref{Line Breaks}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18612
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@,@{@var{c}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18615
msgid ""
"Generate a cedilla accent under @var{c}, as in @,{c}.  @xref{Inserting "
"Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18618
msgid ""
"Insert a discretionary hyphenation point.  @xref{@code{@@- @@hyphenation}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18619
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18622
msgid ""
"Produce a period that ends a sentence (usually after an end-of-sentence "
"capital letter).  @xref{Ending a Sentence}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18623
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@/"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18625
msgid "Produces no output, but allows a line break.  @xref{Line Breaks}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18626
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@:"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18630
msgid ""
"Tell printed output processors to refrain from inserting extra whitespace "
"after an immediately preceding period, question mark, exclamation mark, or "
"colon.  @xref{Not Ending a Sentence}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18631
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@="
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18634
msgid ""
"Generate a macron (bar) accent over the next character, as in @=o.  "
"@xref{Inserting Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18635
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@?"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18638
msgid ""
"Produce a question mark that ends a sentence (usually after an "
"end-of-sentence capital letter).  @xref{Ending a Sentence}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18639
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@@@"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18640
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@atchar@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18642
msgid "Insert an at sign, @samp{@@}.  @xref{Inserting an Atsign}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18643
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@\\"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18644
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@backslashchar@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18648
msgid ""
"Insert a backslash, @samp{\\}; @code{@@backslashchar@{@}} works anywhere, "
"while @code{@@\\} works only inside @code{@@math}.  @xref{Inserting a "
"Backslash}, and @ref{Inserting Math}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18649
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@^"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18650
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@`"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18654
msgid ""
"Generate a circumflex (hat) or grave accent, respectively, over the next "
"character, as in @^o and @`e.  @xref{Inserting Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18655
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@@{"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18656
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@lbracechar@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18658
msgid "Insert a left brace, @samp{@{}.  @xref{Inserting Braces}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18659
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18660
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@rbracechar@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18662
msgid "Insert a right brace, @samp{@}}.  @xref{Inserting Braces}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18663
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@~"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18666
msgid ""
"Generate a tilde accent over the next character, as in @~N.  @xref{Inserting "
"Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18667
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@AA@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18668
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@aa@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18671
msgid ""
"Generate the uppercase and lowercase Scandinavian A-ring letters, "
"respectively: @AA{}, @aa{}.  @xref{Inserting Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18675
msgid ""
"Indicate a general abbreviation, such as `Comput.'.  @xref{@code{@@abbr}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18679
msgid ""
"Indicate an acronym in all capital letters, such as `NASA'.  "
"@xref{@code{@@acronym}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18680
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@AE@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18681
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@ae@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18684
msgid ""
"Generate the uppercase and lowercase AE ligatures, respectively: @AE{}, "
"@ae{}.  @xref{Inserting Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18685
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@afivepaper"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18687
msgid "Change page dimensions for the A5 paper size.  @xref{A4 Paper}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18688
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@afourlatex"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18689
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@afourpaper"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18690
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@afourwide"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18692
msgid "Change page dimensions for the A4 paper size.  @xref{A4 Paper}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18696
msgid ""
"Make the command @samp{@@@var{new}} a synonym for the existing command "
"@samp{@@@var{existing}}.  @xref{@code{@@alias}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18697
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@allowcodebreaks @var{true-false}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18700
msgid ""
"Control breaking at @samp{-} and @samp{_} in printed output.  "
"@xref{@code{@@allowcodebreaks}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18701
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@anchor@{@var{name}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18704
msgid ""
"Define @var{name} as the current location for use as a cross-reference "
"target.  @xref{@code{@@anchor}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18705
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@appendix @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18708
msgid ""
"Begin an appendix.  The title appears in the table of contents.  "
"@xref{@code{@@unnumbered @@appendix}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18709
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@appendixsec @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18710
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@appendixsection @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18715
msgid ""
"Begin an appendix section within an appendix.  The section title appears in "
"the table of contents.  @code{@@appendixsection} is a longer spelling of the "
"@code{@@appendixsec} command.  @xref{@code{@@unnumberedsec @@appendixsec "
"@@heading}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18716
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@appendixsubsec @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18719
msgid ""
"Begin an appendix subsection.  The title appears in the table of contents.  "
"@xref{@code{@@unnumberedsubsec @@appendixsubsec @@subheading}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18720
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@appendixsubsubsec @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18723
msgid ""
"Begin an appendix subsubsection.  The title appears in the table of "
"contents.  @xref{@code{@@subsubsection}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18724
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@arrow@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18727
msgid ""
"Generate a right arrow glyph: @samp{@arrow{}}.  Used by default for "
"@code{@@click}.  @xref{Click Sequences}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18733
msgid ""
"Keep the argument as is.  Used following @code{@@table}, @code{@@ftable}, "
"and @code{@@vtable} to print the table's first column without highlighting "
"(``as is'').  @xref{@code{@@asis}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18734
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@author @var{author}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18737
msgid ""
"Set a manual author in the title page.  @xref{@code{@@title @@subtitle "
"@@author}}.  Set a quotation author in @code{@@quotation}.  "
"@xref{@code{@@quotation}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18738
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@b@{@var{text}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18740
msgid "Set @var{text} in a @b{bold} font, if possible.  @xref{Fonts}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18741
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@bullet@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18744
msgid ""
"Generate a large round dot, @bullet{}, or the closest possible thing to "
"one.  Often used with @code{@@table}.  @xref{@code{@@bullet}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18745
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@bsixpaper"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18747
msgid "Change page dimensions for the B6 paper size.  @xref{A4 Paper}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18748
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@bye"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18751
msgid ""
"Stop processing a file.  The processors do not see anything in the input "
"file following @code{@@bye}.  @xref{Ending a File}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18752
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@c @var{comment}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18756
msgid ""
"Begin a comment in Texinfo.  The rest of the line does not appear in any "
"output.  A synonym for @code{@@comment}.  @kbd{DEL} also starts a comment.  "
"@xref{Comments}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18757
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@caption"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18760
msgid ""
"Define the full caption for a @code{@@float}.  @xref{@code{@@caption "
"@@shortcaption}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18765
msgid ""
"Highlight an example or quotation by drawing a box with rounded corners "
"around it, if possible.  Pair with @code{@@end cartouche}.  "
"@xref{@code{@@cartouche}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18766
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@center @var{line-of-text}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18769
msgid ""
"Center the line of text following the command.  @xref{@code{@@titlefont "
"@@center @@sp}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18770
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@centerchap @var{line-of-text}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18772
msgid ""
"Like @code{@@chapter}, but centers the chapter title.  "
"@xref{@code{@@chapter}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18773
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@chapheading @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18776
msgid ""
"Print an unnumbered chapter-like heading, but omit from the table of "
"contents.  @xref{@code{@@majorheading @@chapheading}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18777
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@chapter @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18780
msgid ""
"Begin a numbered chapter.  The chapter title appears in the table of "
"contents.  @xref{@code{@@chapter}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18781
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@cindex @var{entry}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18784
msgid ""
"Add @var{entry} to the index of concepts.  @xref{Index Entries, , Defining "
"the Entries of an Index}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18788
msgid ""
"Highlight the name of a book or other reference that has no companion Info "
"file.  @xref{@code{@@cite}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18795
msgid ""
"Unset @var{flag}, preventing the Texinfo formatting commands from formatting "
"text between subsequent pairs of @code{@@ifset @var{flag}} and @code{@@end "
"ifset} commands, and preventing @code{@@value@{@var{flag}@}} from expanding "
"to the value to which @var{flag} is set.  @xref{@code{@@set @@clear "
"@@value}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18796
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@click@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18799
msgid ""
"Represent a single ``click'' in a GUI@.  Used within "
"@code{@@clicksequence}.  @xref{Click Sequences}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18800
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@clicksequence@{@var{action} @@click@{@} @var{action}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18802
msgid "Represent a sequence of clicks in a GUI@.  @xref{Click Sequences}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18803
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@clickstyle @@@var{cmd}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18807
msgid ""
"Execute @@@var{cmd} for each @code{@@click}; the default is @code{@@arrow}.  "
"The usual following empty braces on @@@var{cmd} are omitted.  @xref{Click "
"Sequences}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18811
msgid ""
"Indicate an expression, a syntactically complete token of a program, or a "
"program name.  @xref{@code{@@code}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18816
msgid ""
"Control output of @code{`} and @code{'} in code examples.  @xref{Inserting "
"Quote Characters}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18817
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@comma@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18820
msgid ""
"Insert a comma `,' character; only needed when a literal comma would be "
"taken as an argument separator.  @xref{Inserting a Comma}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18823
msgid ""
"Indicate a command name, such as @command{ls}.  @xref{@code{@@command}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18824
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@comment @var{comment}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18828
msgid ""
"Begin a comment in Texinfo.  The rest of the line does not appear in any "
"output.  A synonym for @code{@@c}.  @xref{Comments}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18833
msgid ""
"Print a complete table of contents or specify that a table of content should "
"be output, for formats that may output a table of contents.  @xref{Contents, "
", Generating a Table of Contents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18834
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@copying"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18837
msgid ""
"Specify copyright holders and copying conditions for the document.  Pair "
"with @code{@@end copying}.  @xref{@code{@@copying}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18838
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@copyright@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18841
msgid "Generate the copyright symbol @copyright{}.  @xref{@code{@@copyright}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18842
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@defblock"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18845
msgid ""
"Start a block containing definitions.  Pair with @samp{@@end defblock}.  "
"@xref{Generic Definition Commands}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18846
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@defcodeindex @var{index-name}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18849
msgid ""
"Define a new index and its indexing command.  Print entries in an "
"@code{@@code} font.  @xref{New Indices, , Defining New Indices}."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18851
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@defcvx @var{category} @var{class} @var{name}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18856
msgid ""
"Format a description for a variable associated with a class in "
"object-oriented programming.  Takes three arguments: the category of thing "
"being defined, the class to which it belongs, and its name.  "
"@xref{Definition Commands}."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18858
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@deffnx @var{category} @var{name} @var{arguments}@dots{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18863
msgid ""
"Format a description for a function, interactive command, or similar entity "
"that may take arguments.  @code{@@deffn} takes as arguments the category of "
"entity being described, the name of this particular entity, and its "
"arguments, if any.  @xref{Definition Commands}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18864
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@defindex @var{index-name}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18867
msgid ""
"Define a new index and its indexing command.  Print entries in a roman "
"font.  @xref{New Indices, , Defining New Indices}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:18868
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@definfoenclose @var{newcmd}, @var{before}, @var{after}"
msgstr ""

