#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:20633
#, no-wrap
msgid "Texinfo Mode"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:20635
msgid "@nodedescription Using the GNU Emacs Texinfo mode."
msgstr ""

#. type: appendix
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:20635
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using Texinfo Mode"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:20636
#, no-wrap
msgid "Texinfo mode"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:20637
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mode, using Texinfo"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:20638
#, no-wrap
msgid "GNU Emacs"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:20639
#, no-wrap
msgid "Emacs"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:20645
msgid ""
"You may edit a Texinfo file with any text editor you choose.  A Texinfo file "
"is no different from any other ASCII file.  However, GNU Emacs comes with a "
"special mode, called Texinfo mode, that provides Emacs commands and tools to "
"help ease your work."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:20647 texinfo/texinfo.texi:20649
#, no-wrap
msgid "Texinfo Mode Overview"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:20649
msgid "@nodedescription How Texinfo mode can help you."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:20653
msgid ""
"Texinfo mode provides special features for working with Texinfo files.  You "
"can:"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:20657
msgid "Insert frequently used @@-commands."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:20660
msgid "Automatically create @code{@@node} lines."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:20663
msgid "Show the structure of a Texinfo source file."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:20667
msgid ""
"Automatically create or update the `Next', `Previous', and `Up' pointers of "
"a node."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:20670
msgid "Automatically create or update menus."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:20673
msgid "Automatically create a master menu."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:20676
msgid "Format a part or all of a file for Info."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:20679
msgid "Typeset and print part or all of a file."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:20683
msgid ""
"Perhaps the two most helpful features are those for inserting frequently "
"used @@-commands and for creating node pointers and menus."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:20685
#, no-wrap
msgid "Emacs Editing"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:20687
msgid ""
"@nodedescription Texinfo mode adds to GNU Emacs' general purpose editing "
"features."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:20687
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Usual GNU Emacs Editing Commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:20698
msgid ""
"In most cases, the usual Text mode commands work the same in Texinfo mode as "
"they do in Text mode.  Texinfo mode adds new editing commands and tools to "
"GNU Emacs' general purpose editing features.  The major difference concerns "
"filling.  In Texinfo mode, the paragraph separation variable and syntax "
"table are redefined so that Texinfo commands that should be on lines of "
"their own are not inadvertently included in paragraphs.  Thus, the @kbd{M-q} "
"(@code{fill-paragraph})  command will refill a paragraph but not mix an "
"indexing command on a line adjacent to it into the paragraph."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:20708
msgid ""
"In addition, Texinfo mode sets the @code{page-delimiter} variable to the "
"value of @code{texinfo-chapter-level-regexp}; by default, this is a regular "
"expression matching the commands for chapters and their equivalents, such as "
"appendices.  With this value for the page delimiter, you can jump from "
"chapter title to chapter title with the @kbd{C-x ]} (@code{forward-page}) "
"and @kbd{C-x [} (@code{backward-page}) commands and narrow to a chapter with "
"the @kbd{C-x n p} (@code{narrow-to-page}) command.  (@xref{Pages, , ,emacs, "
"The GNU Emacs Manual}, for details about the page commands.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:20716
msgid ""
"GNU Emacs automatically enters Texinfo mode when you visit a file with a "
"@file{.texinfo}, @file{.texi} or @file{.txi} extension.  Also, Emacs "
"switches to Texinfo mode when you visit a file that has @samp{-*-texinfo-*-} "
"in its first line.  If ever you are in another mode and wish to switch to "
"Texinfo mode, type @code{M-x texinfo-mode}."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:20721
msgid ""
"Like all other Emacs features, you can customize or enhance Texinfo mode as "
"you wish.  In particular, the keybindings are very easy to change.  The "
"keybindings described here are the default or standard ones."
msgstr ""

