#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23395
msgid "Printindex: Info Format Printindex."
msgstr ""

#. type: menuentry
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23395
msgid "Cross-Reference: Info Format Cross Reference"
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23398
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info Format Whole Manual"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23400
msgid "@nodedescription Split vs.@: nonsplit manuals."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23400
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info Format: A Whole Manual"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23402
#, no-wrap
msgid "Nonsplit manuals, Info format of"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23403
#, no-wrap
msgid "Split manuals, Info format of"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23404
#, no-wrap
msgid "Whole manual, in Info format"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23408
msgid ""
"To begin, an Info manual is either @dfn{nonsplit} (contained wholly within a "
"single file) or @dfn{split} (across several files)."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23410
msgid "The syntax for a nonsplit manual is:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23417
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    <nonsplit info file> =\n"
"<preamble>\n"
"<node>*\n"
"<tag table>?\n"
"<local variables>?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23422
msgid ""
"When split, there is a @dfn{main file}, which contains only pointers to the "
"nodes given in other @dfn{subfiles}.  The main file looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23429
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    <split info main file> =\n"
"<preamble>\n"
"<indirect table>\n"
"<tag table>\n"
"<local variables>?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23432
msgid "The subfiles in a split manual have the following syntax:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23437
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    <split info subfile> =\n"
"<preamble>\n"
"<node>*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23441
msgid ""
"Note that the tag table is not optional for split files, as it is used with "
"the indirect table to deduce which subfile a particular node is in."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23444
msgid ""
"Several of the sections in an Info file (such as nodes or tag tables) begin "
"with a sequence:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23447
#, no-wrap
msgid "    <separator> = (^L)?^_(^L)?^J\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23452
msgid ""
"That is, a @samp{CTRL-_} character followed by a newline, with optional "
"formfeed characters."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23455
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info Format Preamble"
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23456
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info Format: Preamble"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23458
#, no-wrap
msgid "Preamble, in Info format"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23463
msgid ""
"The @t{<preamble>} is text at the beginning of all output files.  It is not "
"intended to be visible by default in an Info viewer, but may be displayed "
"upon user request."
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23469
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    <preamble> =\n"
"<identification>       # \"This is FILENAME, produced by ...\"\n"
"<copying text>         # Expansion of @@copying text.\n"
"<dir entries>          # Derived from @@dircategory and @@direntry.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23473
msgid "These pieces are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23475
#, no-wrap
msgid "<identification line>"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23478
msgid ""
"An arbitrary string beginning the output file, followed by a blank line."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23479
#, no-wrap
msgid "<copying text>"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23482
msgid ""
"The expansion of a @code{@@copying} environment, if the manual has one "
"(@pxref{@code{@@copying}})."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23483
#, no-wrap
msgid "<dir entries>"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23486
msgid ""
"The result of any @code{@@dircategory} and @code{@@direntry} commands "
"present in the manual (@pxref{Installing Dir Entries})."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23490
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info Format Indirect Table"
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23491
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info Format: Indirect Table"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23493
#, no-wrap
msgid "Indirect table, in Info format"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23500
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    <indirect table> =\n"
"<separator>\n"
"Indirect:\n"
"(<filename>: <bytepos>)*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23508
msgid ""
"The indirect table is written to the main file in the case of split output "
"only.  It specifies, as a decimal integer, the starting byte position "
"(zero-based) that the first node of each subfile would have if the subfiles "
"were concatenated together in order, not including the top-level file.  The "
"first node of actual content is pointed to by the first entry."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23511
msgid ""
"As an example, suppose split output is generated for the GDB manual.  The "
"top-level file @file{gdb.info} will contain something like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23518
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<separator>\n"
"Indirect:\n"
"gdb.info-1: 1878\n"
"gdb.info-2: 295733\n"
"...\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23525
msgid ""
"This tells Info viewers that the first node of the manual occurs at byte "
"1878 of the file @file{gdb.info-1} (which would be after that file's "
"preamble.)  The first node in the @file{gdb.info-2} subfile would start at "
"byte 295733 if @file{gdb.info-2} were appended to @file{gdb.info-1}, "
"including any preamble sections in both files."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23531
msgid ""
"Unfortunately, Info-creating programs such as @command{makeinfo} have not "
"always implemented these rules perfectly, due to various bugs and "
"oversights.  Therefore, robust Info viewers should fall back to searching "
"``nearby'' the given position for a node, instead of giving up immediately "
"if the position is not exactly at a node beginning."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23533
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info Format Tag Table"
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23534
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info Format: Tag Table"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23536
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tag table, in Info format"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23546
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    <tag table> =\n"
"<separator>\n"
"Tag Table:\n"
"(<lparen>Indirect<rparen>)?\n"
"(Node|Ref): <nodeid>^?<bytepos>\n"
"<separator>\n"
"End Tag Table\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23549
msgid "The @samp{(Indirect)} line appears in the case of split output only."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23553
msgid ""
"The tag table specifies the starting byte position of each node and anchor "
"in the file.  In the case of split output, it is only written in the main "
"output file."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23559
msgid ""
"Each line defines an identifier as either an anchor or a node, as "
"specified.  For example, @samp{Node: Top^?1647} says that the node named "
"@samp{Top} starts at byte 1647 while @samp{Ref: Overview-Footnote-1^?30045} "
"says that the anchor named @samp{Overview-Footnote-1} starts at byte 30045.  "
"It is an error to define the same identifier both ways."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23564
msgid ""
"In the case of nonsplit output, the byte positions simply refer to the "
"location in the output file.  In the case of split output, the byte "
"positions refer to an imaginary file created by concatenating all the split "
"files (but not the top-level file).  See the previous section."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23566 texinfo/texinfo.texi:23763
msgid "Here is an example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23574
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"^_\n"
"Tag Table:\n"
"Node: Top^?89\n"
"Node: Ch1^?292\n"
"^_\n"
"End Tag Table\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23580
msgid ""
"This specifies a manual with two nodes, `Top' and `Ch1', at byte positions "
"89 and 292 respectively.  Because the @samp{(Indirect)} line is not present, "
"the manual is not split."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23583
msgid ""
"Preamble sections or other non-node sections of files do not have a tag "
"table entry."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23585
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info Format Local Variables"
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23586
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info Format: Local Variables"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23588
#, no-wrap
msgid "Local variable section, in Info format"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23592
msgid ""
"The local variables section is optional and is currently used to give the "
"encoding information.  It may be augmented in the future."
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23599
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    <local variables> =\n"
"<separator>\n"
"Local Variables:\n"
"coding: <encoding>\n"
"End:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23602
msgid "@xref{@code{@@documentencoding}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23604
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info Format Regular Nodes"
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23605
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info Format: Regular Nodes"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23607
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info nodes, in Info format"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23610
msgid "Regular nodes look like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23615
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    <node> =\n"
"<separator>\n"
"File: <fn>, Node: <id1>, (Next: <id2>, )? (Prev: <id3>, )? Up: <id4>\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23617
#, no-wrap
msgid "<general text, until the next ^_ or end-of-file>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23623
msgid ""
"At least one space or tab must be present after each colon and comma, but "
"any number of spaces are ignored.  The @t{<id>} node identifiers have "
"following format:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23628
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   <id> = (<lparen><infofile><rparen>)?<node-spec>?\n"
"   <node-spec> = <nodename> | <del><nodename><del>\n"
"   <del> = ^?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23633
msgid ""
"This @t{<node>} defines @t{<id1>} in file @t{<fn>}, which is typically "
"either @samp{manualname} or @samp{manualname.info}.  No parenthesized "
"@t{<infofile>} component may appear within @t{<id1>}."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23640
msgid ""
"Each of the identifiers after @code{Next}, @code{Prev} and @code{Up} refer "
"to nodes or anchors within a file.  These pointers normally refer within the "
"same file, but @samp{(dir)} is often used to point to the top-level dir "
"file.  If an @t{<infofile>} component is used then the node name may be "
"omitted, in which case the node identifier refers to the @samp{Top} node "
"within the referenced file."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23646
msgid ""
"The @code{Next} and @code{Prev} pointers are optional.  The @code{Up} "
"pointer is technically also optional, although most likely this indicates a "
"mistake in the node structuring.  Conventionally, the nodes are arranged to "
"form a tree, but this is not a requirement of the format."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23653
msgid ""
"Node names containing periods, commas, colons or parentheses can confuse "
"Info readers.  If it is necessary to refer to a node whose name contains any "
"of these, the @t{<nodename>} should be surrounded by a pair of @code{DEL} "
"characters (@samp{CTRL-?}, character number 127).  @command{makeinfo} adds "
"these characters when needed in the default case.  Note that not all Info "
"readers recognize this syntax.  @xref{Info Node Names Constraints}."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23656
msgid ""
"The @t{<general text>} of the node can include the special constructs "
"described next."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23658
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info Format Menu"
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23659
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info Format: Menu"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23661
#, no-wrap
msgid "Menus, in Info format"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23665
msgid ""
"Conventionally menus appear at the end of nodes, but the Info format places "
"no restrictions on their location."
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23670
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    <menu> =\n"
"* Menu:\n"
"(<menu entry> | <menu comment>)*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23677
msgid ""
"The parts of a @t{<menu entry>} are also described in @ref{Menu Parts}.  "
"They have the same syntax as cross-references, with a leading @samp{*} "
"instead of @samp{* (N|n)ote} (@pxref{Info Format Cross Reference}).  Indices "
"extend the menu format to specify the destination line; @pxref{Info Format "
"Printindex}."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23682
msgid ""
"A @t{<menu comment>} is any line not beginning with @samp{*} that appears "
"either at the beginning of the menu or is separated from a menu entry by one "
"or more blank lines.  These comments are intended to be displayed as part of "
"the menu, as-is (@pxref{Writing a Menu})."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23684
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info Format Image"
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23685
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info Format: Image"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23687
#, no-wrap
msgid "Images @subentry in Info format"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23691
msgid ""
"The @code{@@image} command results in the following special directive within "
"the Info file (@pxref{Images}):"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23698
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    <image> =\n"
"^@@^H[image src=\"<image file>\"\n"
"            (text=\"<txt file contents>\")?\n"
"            (alt=\"<alt text>\")?\n"
"^@@^H]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23703
msgid ""
"The line breaks and indentation in this description are editorial; the "
"whitespace between the different parts of the directive in Info files is "
"arbitrary."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23707
msgid ""
"In the strings @t{<image file>}, @t{<txt file contents>} and @t{<alt text>}, "
"@samp{\"} is quoted as @samp{\\\"} and @samp{\\} is quoted as @samp{\\\\}.  "
"The txt and alt specifications are optional."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23712
msgid ""
"The @t{alt} value serves the same purpose as in HTML: A prose description of "
"the image.  In text-only displays or speech systems, for example, the "
"@t{alt} value may be used instead of displaying the (typically graphical) "
"@t{<image file>}."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23715
msgid ""
"The @t{<txt file contents>}, if present, should be taken as an ASCII "
"representation of the image, for possible use on a text-only display."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23718
msgid ""
"The format does not prescribe the choice between displaying the @t{<image "
"file>}, the @t{<alt text>} or the @t{<txt file contents>}."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23720
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info Format Printindex"
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23721
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info Format: Printindex"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23723
#, no-wrap
msgid "Indices, in Info format"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23727
msgid ""
"An index in Info format is a kind of menu, with an additional directive at "
"the beginning to mark it as an index menu."
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23732
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    <printindex> =\n"
"^@@^H[index^@@^H]\n"
"* Menu:\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23734
#, no-wrap
msgid "<index entry>*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23739
msgid ""
"The @t{<index entry>} items are similar to normal menu entries, but the "
"free-format description is replaced by the line number of where the entries "
"occurs in the text:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23743
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    <index entry> =\n"
"* <entry text>: <node-spec>. <line-spec>\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23746
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    <line-spec> =\n"
"<lparen>line <lineno><rparen>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23752
msgid ""
"The initial part, @samp{<entry text>: <entry node>.}, should be on a single "
"line.  The @t{<entry text>} is the index term."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23757
msgid ""
"Even though @t{<entry text>} is followed by a colon, it may itself contain "
"colons, so Info readers should try to include as much of the line as "
"possible in the @t{<entry text>}.  (However, @t{<entry text>} may not "
"contain the @code{DEL} characters that may occur in @t{<node-spec>}.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23761
msgid ""
"@t{<lineno>} is an unsigned integer, given relative to the start of the "
"@t{<entry node>}.  An optional line break may occur before "
"@samp{<line-spec>}."
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23767
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"^@@^H[index^@@^H]\n"
"* Menu:\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23769
#, no-wrap
msgid "* thunder:           Weather Phenomena.             (line 5)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23773
msgid ""
"This means that an index entry for `thunder' appears at line 5 of the node "
"`Weather Phenomena'."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23775
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info Format Cross Reference"
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23776
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info Format: Cross-reference"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23778
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cross-references, in Info format"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23781
msgid ""
"A general cross-reference in Info format has one of the following two forms:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23787
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    <cross-reference> =\n"
"  * (N|n)ote <id>::\n"
"| * (N|n)ote <label>:<id>(.|,)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23790
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    <id> = (<lparen><infofile><rparen>)?<node-spec>?\n"
"    <label> = <label text> | <del><label text><del>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23798
msgid ""
"No space should occur between the @samp{*} character and the following "
"@samp{N} or @samp{n}.  @samp{*Note} should be used at the start of a "
"sentence, otherwise @samp{*note} should be used.  (Some Info readers, such "
"as the one in Emacs, can display @samp{*Note} and @samp{*note} as @samp{See} "
"and @samp{see} respectively.) In both cases, @t{<label text>} is descriptive "
"text."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23804
msgid ""
"In both forms the @t{<id>} refers to a node or anchor, in the same way as a "
"reference in the node information line does (@pxref{Info Format Regular "
"Nodes}).  The optional parenthesized @samp{<infofile>} is the name of the "
"manual being referenced, and @t{<node-spec>} gives the node or anchor within "
"that manual."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23808
msgid ""
"The second form has a descriptive label.  A cross-reference in this form "
"should usually be terminated with a comma or period, to make it feasible to "
"find the end of the @t{<id>}."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23816
msgid ""
"If @t{<label>} contains a colon character (@t{:}), it should be surrounded "
"with a pair of @t{<del>} characters.  Likewise, quoting characters may be "
"used for the node name if it contains problematic characters; then a "
"terminating comma or period is not needed.  As stated earlier, this quoting "
"mechanism is not supported in all Info-reading programs."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23819
msgid ""
"The format does not prescribe how to find other manuals to resolve such "
"references."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23821
msgid "Here are some examples:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23828
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*note GNU Free Documentation License::\n"
"*note Tag table: Info Format Tag Table, for details.\n"
"*Note Overview: (make)Top.\n"
"*Note ^?:^?: (bash)Bourne Shell Builtins.\n"
"*Note alloca.h: (gnulib)^?alloca.h^?.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23832
msgid ""
"The first shows a reference to a node in the current manual using the short "
"form."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23837
msgid ""
"The second also refers to a node in the current manual, namely `Info Format "
"Tag Table'; the `Tag table' before the @samp{:} is only a label on this "
"particular reference, and the @samp{for details.} is text belonging to the "
"sentence, not part of the reference."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23840
msgid ""
"The third example refers to the node `Top' in another manual, namely "
"@samp{make}, with `Overview' being the label for this cross-reference."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23843
msgid ""
"The fourth example shows a colon character being quoted in a label, and the "
"fifth example shows a period being quoted in a node name."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23845
msgid "@xref{Cross References}."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23849
msgid "@nodedescription Copying this manual."
msgstr ""

#. type: unnumbered
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23854 texinfo/texinfo.texi:23855
#, no-wrap
msgid "Command and Variable Index"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23860
msgid ""
"This is an alphabetical list of all the @@-commands, assorted Emacs Lisp "
"functions, and several variables.  To make the list easier to use, the "
"commands are listed without their preceding @samp{@@}."
msgstr ""

#. type: unnumbered
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23864 texinfo/texinfo.texi:23866
#, no-wrap
msgid "General Index"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo.texi:23866
msgid "@nodedescription A menu covering many topics."
msgstr ""
